Z||000000||Cheever3000||09-09-2001||05:08 PM||||Home from the Bud Classic last light, taking my car off the trailer, some long spring got hung up on the ramp, and now the clutch pedal has no resistance.<P>Did a quick search, but haven't looked in the Haynes book or the PFF CD yet.  Still hoping someone would know exactly what I broke and what to do about it.  Do you?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-09-2001||05:51 PM||||Spring?  How big(dia)... could it be part of the used-to-be protective spring-like hard hydraulic line busted apart?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">   <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||09-09-2001||05:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>Spring?  How big... could it be par of the protective spring-like hard hydraulic line busted apart?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That would be my guess too, although I hope that isn't it (PITA to change).<P>Check your clutch master cylinder to see if it is low/empty......also look for a puddle of fluid under the car.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||09-09-2001||05:55 PM||||Sounds Like your hydrolic line. It has a protective spring around it. About a 1/4 inch ID? 3/8th OD? Below rear drivers side wheel?<BR>Coy. <BR>Wow Everyone posted at once.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 09-09-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000004||JetroGT||09-09-2001||06:53 PM||||Make sure that the pin on the clutch pedel is still attatched to the plunger on the master cylinder.<BR>Happened to  me  once.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/New_Banner1.jpg"> <P>I work where all the missing paperclips go.||||reg||1
